                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[hr][/hr] \n[h2]The Positive:[/h2] \n\nIt was a type of game that was somehow a bit fun, because it was such a fever dream to play.\n\n[hr][/hr] \n[h2]The Neutral:[/h2] \n\nThe story seems to have been written by a very religious person.\n\n[hr][/hr] \n[h2]The Negative:[/h2] \n\nAll of the voice actors were clearly amateurs, one of them in particular drives me crazy: Pandora.\n\nSome of the puzzles are at nonsensical to me, where I only got through with the walkthrough, as there were no hints, seemed like you would have to trial and error it.\n\nThe visuals are positively ancient.\n\nSome of the things you have to find are stupidly small on the screen and you might as well just screen the screen with your mouse to find stuff you can interact with.\n\nThe resolution for me was stuck in a very small thing and it didnt stretch out, just kept being like a quarter of my screen.\n\nThe Steam overlay glitched out completely, where I could somewhat use it, but anything coming from it (including notifications!) was half-way stuck on the screen until you restarted the game. Not as bad, since most of your screen isnt used anyways, but still, wtf.\n\nHad one nasty crash, where I had to navigate blindly on Desktop 2 to get the game to close, because it wasnt a window anymore, just something blocking the screen for some reason, while not pressing windows+tab.\n\n[hr][/hr] \nIm on a quest of at least trying every game in my library, of which I got plenty from all kinds of bundles. If you are interested in my journey, check out my other reviews :)",
